# Vercel serves root files statically, so anything uploaded here can become
# fetchable. Git-connected deploys only ever ship committed files, but a CLI
# deploy (`vercel deploy`) uploads from the working directory — which in this
# repo contains untracked side projects holding live API tokens.
#
# Keep this in sync with .gitignore.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Real client data. Files under api/ are served statically, so a deployed dossier
# would be publicly fetchable at /api/<filename>.
api/*.txt
api/Dossier*

# Standalone side projects that live here but are not part of the deployed app
hubspot-setup/
serp-mvp/
sales-handoff/
kit-host/
post-suspension/
Documents/

# Local dev server — never runs on Vercel
local/

# Junk
node_modules/
main
screen5_backup_COMPLETE.html
.git/
